      "timelineId": "moonstone-timeline-main",
      "number": 45,
      "title": "Second Period, Third Narrative — Franklin Blake: Chapter 10",
      "synopsis": "Franklin visits the ailing doctor and notices that Ezra Jennings can interpret fragments left by fever. The assistant assembles the shorthand record showing that Candy secretly dosed Franklin with opium after their argument. Ezra argues that a controlled repetition of place, fatigue, and opium may reproduce Franklin’s automatic act.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
    },
    {
      "worldId": "moonstone-world",
      "createdAt": 1786464000000,
      "updatedAt": 1786464000000,
      "id": "moonstone-chapter-046",
      "timelineId": "moonstone-timeline-main",
      "number": 46,
      "title": "Second Period, Fourth Narrative — Ezra Jennings’s Journal",
      "synopsis": "Ezra’s journal records furniture, rooms, sleep deprivation, and the mock diamond arranged to match the birthday conditions. Rachel returns against the formal plan and takes a hidden place from which she can witness Franklin’s second passage. Under opium, Franklin takes the mock stone from Rachel’s room and carries it away without waking knowledge. The journal preserves each dose, interval, and action so the result does not depend on sympathetic recollection.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
    },
    {
      "worldId": "moonstone-world",
      "createdAt": 1786464000000,
      "updatedAt": 1786464000000,
      "id": "moonstone-chapter-047",
      "timelineId": "moonstone-timeline-main",
      "number": 47,
      "title": "Second Period, Fifth Narrative — Franklin Blake",
      "synopsis": "Franklin resumes the story after the journal; he and Rachel acknowledge love while the diamond itself remains missing. Back in London, the bank receipt and loan date show that the pledged stone will leave the strongroom. Sergeant Cuff joins the London pursuit, admits the limit of his first solution, and seals a new prediction. The boy watches Luker’s movements and identifies a disguised man who receives the recovered diamond. At the Wheel of Fortune, the investigators discover the carrier murdered and expose the disguise as Godfrey Ablewhite’s.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
    },
