      "id": "moonstone-chapter-057",
      "timelineId": "moonstone-timeline-main",
      "number": 57,
      "title": "Epilogue — Statement of Mr Murthwaite",
      "synopsis": "Travelling in western India, Murthwaite joins thousands of pilgrims converging on Somnauth and recognizes figures from the English pursuit. The crowd moves toward the ancient city as music and ceremony draw the scattered procession together. The three custodians complete their shared service and prepare for separate lifelong pilgrimages. Near Somnauth, Murthwaite witnesses the three guardians’ completed service as the diamond shines again above the pilgrims.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
